From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: michael moore <mrmoore27@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 01:10:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] prime, split-only patch: probe advertisers too; the C
 gateway keeps zero-value outputs after its payees

The readiness demo ran the split-only datum_gateway live for the first time.
It advertised nta-v1, parsed the 70-byte attestations, and then dropped them
all: generate_coinbase_txns_for_stratum_job_subtypebysize stopped adding
outputs once the payees had used the coinbase value, and every attestation is
a zero-value output after them. Prime caught it on the first post-activation
share (attestations dropped) and refused it. Both loops now go on past the
spent value; the value check still admits only zero-value outputs there.

So the flag is a claim, not evidence. Prime now probes every gateway before
activation, advertiser or not, and a dropped probe outranks the flag. A build
that dropped while advertising is not believed again until it says hello with
another user agent (an upgrade); a reconnect of the same build stays refused.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
