 #   XBT-NTA capability (SOV-011). The hello carries "nta-v1\0" right after the
 #   4-byte header key seed, where stock sends only random padding (stock
 #   datum_protocol.c:1028-1033; every server skips it). Lazarus Prime reads it as
-#   "keeps 70-byte attestation outputs" and does not probe the gateway before NTA
-#   activation; a gateway without it is probed and, if it drops the probe,
-#   refused work from the activation height.
+#   "keeps 70-byte attestation outputs": ready. It still probes the gateway
+#   before NTA activation, and one that drops the probe (flag or not) is refused
+#   work from the activation height.
+#
+#   Zero-value outputs after the payees (SOV-011). generate_coinbase_txns_for_
+#   stratum_job_subtypebysize no longer stops once the payees have used the
+#   coinbase value: the XBT-NTA attestations (and a Prime's pre-activation
+#   probe) come after the payees and are zero-value, and stopping there dropped
+#   them all, so every post-activation block was bad-nta-count. Found live by
+#   the SOV-011 readiness demo: the gateway advertised nta-v1 and Prime refused
+#   it after its first post-activation share.
 #
